# Contributing to {{ project_name }}

Thanks for contributing!

## Setup

```bash
just install
```

## Before you open a PR

- `just qa` must pass (lint, type-check, tests).
- Add tests for new behavior (see `agent-guidelines/testing.md`).
- Update `CHANGELOG.md` under `[Unreleased]`.
- Update docs where relevant (see `agent-guidelines/documentation.md`).

Pre-commit runs automatically on every commit. Run all hooks manually with
`just lint`.

## Notes for editors

- `docs/skills/` is a **symlink** to the top-level `skills/` directory (set
  during `copier copy`). Don't delete or commit the resolved files — edit the
  originals under `skills/` and let MkDocs follow the link. If the symlink is
  ever lost, re-create it with `ln -s ../skills docs/skills` (Unix/WSL2 only).
{%- if 'codex' in coding_agents or 'pi' in coding_agents %}
- `.agents/skills/` is the native Codex/Pi discovery symlink to the same
  top-level `skills/` directory. Re-create it with
  `mkdir -p .agents && ln -s ../skills .agents/skills` if it is lost.
{%- endif %}
- **Bumping Ruff (or another tool used both from `uv.lock` and Pre-Commit)** —
  update the lockfile and the hook's immutable commit SHA plus readable release
  comment in the same commit. `pre-commit autoupdate` may restore a mutable tag;
  resolve that release tag to its reviewed commit before merging. Run `just qa`
  after both sides are synchronized.
